WEBVTT

cue-1
00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.099
-[Outro music playing]
-What?

cue-2
00:00:01.939 --> 00:00:06.919
Not another bill. For printing handbills
and for ballad singers? A necessary

cue-3
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:11.599
expense, I suppose. But this election's
costing a fortune. We've had money from

cue-4
00:00:11.599 --> 00:00:16.178
all over England, but it's mostly me that
seems to be paying. I don't have

cue-5
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.359
government money pouring into my pockets
like the new interest does. And now the

cue-6
00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:25.519
polling's started, I'll probably be here
for days. Well, I suppose it's the first

cue-7
00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:28.520
time the people have had a chance to vote
for members of Parliament in over 40

cue-8
00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:33.360
years. They want to make the most of it.
But one thing's for sure, I won't be able

cue-9
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.539
to afford this again, even if the next
contest isn't for another 40 years.
